{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>In one house it shall be eaten.</b> According to the plain sense: in a house — each and every person's father's house it shall be eaten, and they shall not send portions from it, one man to his fellow, for this is not the way of haste but the way of people seated at a fixed meal. Or, lest the destroyer encounter them. And so it is written: ״ואתם לא תצאו איש מפתח ביתו עד בוקר״." "<b>And a bone you shall not break.</b> To take out the marrow from it, lest you come to delay, for the entire matter is in the manner of haste. Another interpretation: <b>and a bone you shall not break in it</b> — since it is eaten in a group and it is proper for each one to take his portion, Scripture tells you that no man should object to the division of the bone, and one may not break it. Another interpretation: its law was to be eaten when satiated, so that the taste of the pesach would be in his mouth; if one breaks a bone in it, it looks like the behavior of a starving glutton. And one may say: the reason it is eaten when satiated is precisely so that one not come to break a bone. And one should not object: let it rather be eaten for appetite, so that one not come to leftover. For leftover has a remedy through burning, unlike breaking. <b>And a bone you shall not break.</b> And if you ask: let the positive commandment of ״ואכלו את הבשר״ come and set aside the negative commandment of ״ועצם לא תשברו בו״? — the negative commandment does not need to be stated, for the prohibition of breaking has already been stated in ״ככל חוקת הפסח יעשו אותו״. This means: both a bone that has marrow and a bone that has no marrow but has upon it an olive's-bulk of flesh — there is in it the prohibition of breaking a bone. Thus is the mishnah in chapter כיצד צולין."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "The phrase הוי אומר introducing the baraita at the end is rendered as 'This means'; the syntax is elliptic and the clause reading is somewhat uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:35.120426840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}